title: 'pallet-assets: allow force_create to set an arbitrary asset id when auto-increment is enabled'

doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    `force_create` no longer requires the asset id to equal `NextAssetId`: a `ForceOrigin` may
    create an asset with any id not currently in use. When auto-increment is active and the chosen
    id is at or beyond `NextAssetId`, the sequence is advanced past it so it can never later
    collide; ids below `NextAssetId` are left for deliberate assignment.

    Auto-increment is handled inside the pallet, gated only by `NextAssetId` being set (via
    genesis or the `SetNextAssetId` migration). The `AutoIncAssetId` callback type is removed; do
    not drive auto-increment through `Config::CallbackHandle`.

    Migration: `Config::AssetId` now requires `Incrementable + PartialOrd`. Integer ids already
    satisfy this; `Location` gains an `Incrementable` impl whose `increment` returns `None`,
    keeping auto-increment disabled for `Location`-keyed assets. Runtimes that set
    `CallbackHandle = AutoIncAssetId<..>` must drop it and instead initialize `NextAssetId`.

